"hadiths[353]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2722,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the major Hajj is on the day of sacrifice and the minor Hajj is Umrah.
2723,"Abu Bakr bin Muhammad narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father. ""Umrah is a short Hajj and the Qur'an can only be touched by an ablution person""."
2724,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may God be pleased with him) narrates that a person asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the prayer of Zakat and Hajj. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Yes.” It is portable."
2725,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, but if you perform Umrah, it is better for you."
2726,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2727,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, I asked, O Messenger of Allah, is it obligatory to perform Umrah and is it obligatory like Hajj? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, but if you perform Umrah, it is better for you."
2728,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) told her about her Umrah, i.e. the Umrah performed by Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, that the reward for your Umrah will be based on what you have spent."
2729,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked her about her Umrah.
2730,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a person who performs Umrah will continue to read Talbiyah until he starts Tawaf.
2731,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the person who performs Hajj by combining Umrah with Hajj.
2732,"Saeed Ibn Musaib narrates that Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Uthman (RA) both came for Hajj. On the way, Sayyidna Uthman (RA) forbade Umrah to be added to Hajj as a ritual. But Sayyidna Uthman did not forbid these gentlemen, Sayyidna Ali (RA) said, ""I know that you have forbidden them to perform Umrah together as a form of Tamattu."" He replied, ""Yes!"" So Sayyiduna Ali said to him, ""Haven't you heard this, then you have enjoyed the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"" So they answered yes."
2733,"Saeed bin Musayyib narrates that on the way to Hajj, Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) was told to Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) that Sayyidna 'Uthman had forbidden his companions from combining Umrah with Hajj, that is, from performing Hajj, so Sayyidna 'Ali said to his companions: When Sayyidna 'Uthman departs, you will also depart. The narrator narrates that then Sayyiduna Ali and his companions put on Ihram for Umrah, Sayyiduna Uthman did not say anything to them: Sayyiduna Ali said to Sayyiduna Uthman: I have been told this about you: You have forbidden your companions from combining Umrah with Hajj, i.e. performing Hajj Tamattu. So Syedna Usman replied yes. Saeed narrates, I do not know what Syedna Usman replied to him."
2734,"Sayyiduna Anas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) read this. ""I am here to perform Hajj and Umrah together."" This tradition is narrated along with another document."
2735,"Abdullah bin Abu Qadah narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Hajj and Umrah, knowing that he would not perform Hajj after that."
2736,"Abdullah bin Abu Malikah narrates that a person came to the service of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas asked him where you came from. He replied, ""I am drinking Zam Zam water."" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas asked him, ""Did you drink it as it should have been drunk?"" He asked, ""O Sayyidna Ibn Abbas, how is it (drinking)?"" Then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas said, ""When you drink it, turn towards the Qiblah and recite the name of Allah, and then drink it in three breaths and drink it in large quantities when you drink it, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recites the praises of Allah."" Peace be upon him has said that the main difference between us and the hypocrites is that they (hypocrites) do not drink zam-zam in large quantities."
2737,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2738,"Ikrama narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) used to say this dua when he drank Zam Zam water. ""O Allah! I ask You for knowledge that gives benefit, I ask for sustenance that is vast, and I ask for healing from every disease."
2739,"Mujahid narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you drink the water of Zam-Zam, if you drink it because you will be healed by it, then Allah will bless you with healing. The result is and through this Allah watered Sayyidna Ismail."
2740,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touching his blessed face and his chest with that of Multzam.
2741,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) placed his forehead on the Black Stone.
2742,"Ata narrates that I saw Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri, Abu Huraira, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, and Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu, these gentlemen used to kiss their hands when receiving the Black Stone. The narrator narrates, I inquired if you have seen Sayyidna Ibn Abbas doing this too, so he replied, I have seen Sayyidna Ibn Abbas doing this many times."
2743,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to kiss the Yamani man and he would place his blessed face on it.
2744,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah has quoted this saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that it is lawful for you to hunt dry land while you are in the state of Ihram, when you have not hunted it yourself, and it has not been hunted by you."
2745,This tradition is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir along with another chain of transmission.
2746,This tradition is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) along with another chain of transmission.
2747,This same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission from Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him).
2748,The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) along with another chain of transmission.
2749,"Abdullah bin Abu Qatadah narrates this statement from his father (Sayyidna Abu Qatadah, may Allah be pleased with him) on the occasion of Hudaybiyyah, I went with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (to perform Umrah), my companions put on Ihram, but I did not put on Ihram, I saw a blue cow and attacked it and hunted it, then I narrated this incident to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioning that I was not wearing Ihram at that time and I have hunted it for you, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his companions to eat that meat, but the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not eat it because I had told you that I had hunted it for you. These are the words of the hadith, I have hunted for you and these words the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not eat, it was mentioned only by a narrator named Muammar. All Muslims agree on this. Believers! Do not kill the victim when you are in the state of Ihram."
2750,"Yahya bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this statement of his father. He performed Umrah with Sayyidna Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, along with a few others. They offered a bird to Sayyidna Uthman, so Sayyidna Uthman said to the others: Let them eat it, and he refused to eat it. So Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) replied that my position regarding him is not like yours, he has been hunted for me."
2751,"Abu Umamah Taymi narrates: I said to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: I rent things like this, now they say that your Hajj has not been done? So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said, “A man came to the Prophet (PBUH) and he (PBUH) inquired about the matter about which you asked me: Yes, the Prophet (PBUH) remained silent until this verse was revealed. ""There is no sin on you when you seek the grace of your Lord."" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Your Hajj has been completed."""
2752,"Abu Umamah Taymi narrates: I said to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar: I give (riding animals) (to the pilgrims) on rent. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrated a tradition similar to this regarding the Prophet (PBUH) and he said, ""You are a Haji."""
2753,This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA).
2754,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about a person who had been slaughtered before sacrificing his head, but before offering sacrifice, the Prophet (PBUH) kept saying that there is no harm in it, there is no harm in it."
2755,Alaa bin Musayb narrates this with reference to a person belonging to Banutim.
2756,"Abu Umamah Taymi narrates: I said to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): If we rent (animals to pilgrims), will our Hajj be performed? So Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar Radiyallahu Anhuma said, ""Don't you people circumambulate the House of Allah, don't you go to Arafat field, don't you throw pebbles at Jamrat, and don't you shave your head?"" We replied yes! So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said, “A man came to the Prophet (PBUH) and asked him about the same thing that he had asked me, but the Prophet (PBUH) did not answer him until Gabriel came down with this verse. ""There is no sin on you if you seek the grace of your Lord."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""You people are pilgrims."""
2757,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas (Radi Allahu Anhu) (the narrator says) has narrated this as a hadeeth, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one should ever say that I will remain single."
2758,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) forbade a Muslim called a single (monk) to go.
2759,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that I cursed the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that at that time he was giving the sermon of Hajj Al-Wada to the people on his camel. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Obey your Lord, perform the five prayers, pay Zakat on your wealth, observe the fasts of your appointed month, obey your rulers and enter the Paradise of your Lord."" Narrator narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, how many years ago did you hear this hadith? He replied, I was thirty years old at that time."
2760,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that a woman should keep her face uncovered in Ihram.
2761,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) said that a woman will cover her face in Ihram and a man will cover his head in Ihram.
2762,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: We (women) set out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we were in the state of Ihram.
2763,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa narrates: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we were in the state of Ihram. When we encountered a rider, we would put the cloth on our heads in front of our faces and when he passed by, we would remove it."
2764,Sayyidah Umm Salma (RA) narrates: We were with the Prophet (PBUH) and we were in the state of Ihram.
2765,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person fell from his camel, he was in the state of Ihram, he passed away, the Prophet (PBUH) ordered about him that he will be shrouded in these two clothes, he will be bathed but his face should not be covered, he will be perfumed, and he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection while reciting Talbiyah."
2766,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says that it is not necessary for women to perform the Tawaf of Baytullah and the Sa'i of Safa and Marwah.
2767,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a woman will not climb directly above Safa and Marwah, and she will not raise her voice while reciting Talbiyah. In one tradition, only these words are said: A woman will not climb over Safawmruh."
2768,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that it is not obligatory for women to run between Baitullah (during Tawaf) and Safa and Marwah.
2769,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person fell off his horse in the morning of the day of Arafah and he was in the state of Ihram. He died. This was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said, ""Ghusl him with water and berry leaves, and shroud him in the same two clothes, and do not cover his face, because he will be alive on the Day of Resurrection reciting Talbiyah."""
2770,"The same hadith is narrated along with another document, but it contains these words and it is not Sarkodhanpana."
2771,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: We were traveling with the Prophet (PBUH) and a man fell from his camel and died. He was in the state of Ihram.
2772,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this about a person who dies in the state of Ihram, you should cover him and do not resemble the Jews."
2773,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2774,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person was accompanying the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the state of Ihram and he fell from his camel, his neck bone was broken and he died. A narrator named Ibn Jaraj narrates, I asked my teacher, did Saeed bin Jubayr tell you about the place where that person fell? So he answered no!"
2775,This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads.
2776,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cover the faces of your men and do not resemble the Jews.
2777,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) A person was following the Prophet (PBUH) in the state of Ihram, he fell from his camel, his neck bone was broken, and he died."
2778,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2779,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that whoever performs Hajj or Umrah dies in this state (i.e. the state of Ihram), then he will not appear and will not be counted from him, and said to him: You will enter Paradise."
2780,"Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajrah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) saw that his lice were falling on his face. This is about the location of Hudaybiyah. The Prophet (PBUH) asked him, ""Are your lice bothering you?"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to be leaders, even though they were at Hudaybiyyah at that time and the Prophet had not yet announced to the people that he would open Ihram here, because the people wanted him to enter Makkah. Then Allah revealed the order of redemption. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed them to divide one, the difference, among six poor people or sacrifice a goat or fast for three days."
2781,"Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajrah (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) passed by him, he was lighting a fire under his hand. Narrator named Sufyan narrates (about this event) this verse was revealed: ""So whoever among you is sick or has a headache, let him give an offering."""
2782,"Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajrah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) saw that his lice were falling on his face. This is about the location of Hudaybiyah. The Prophet (PBUH) asked him, ""Are your lice bothering you?"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to be leaders, even though they were at the place of Hudaybiyyah at that time and the Prophet had not yet announced to the people that he would open Ihram here because the people wanted him to enter Makkah. Then Allah sent down the order of redemption, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed them to divide one, the difference, among six poor people or sacrifice an animal or fast for three days."
2783,"Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajra (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) passed by him and he was lighting a fire under his hand. This is about Hudaybiyah. The Prophet (PBUH) asked him if your lice were bothering you. (The narrator narrates) So this verse was revealed: ""So whoever among you is sick or has a headache, he should fast as a ransom or give charity or sacrifice."" The order of fasting is to fast for three days. Sadaqah means that six poor people should be given one, a difference, and Qurbani means that a goat should be sacrificed."
2784,"Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajra (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) passed by him, his hair was big at the roots of his hair and there were lice in the upper part of his hair. He said no! The Prophet said: Then if you wish, fast for three days, feed three sa's of dates (to the poor) and give one sa' to each poor person."
2785,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says about a person in the state of Ihram who trims his nails, he will feed a sa'a of grain from each palm."
2786,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that people used to go back to wherever they were going from Mina. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed them to perform Tawaf of the House of Allah at the end (and go home from there).
2787,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this as a hadeeth: He who eats the rent of houses in Makkah eats fire.
2788,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates that the method of throwing pebbles is to say Takbeer along with it.
2789,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: We said, O Messenger of Allah, we believe that the number of pebbles that are thrown at the Jamrats every year will be exhausted. The Prophet (PBUH) said, ""Those that are accepted will be picked up. If it is possible, you will see (heaps of pebbles) here like mountains."""
2790,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when a person completes his Hajj, he should return to his home as soon as possible because his reward is high."
2791,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""When a man returns from a journey and brings a gift for his wife, he should give her a gift, even if it is a stone."""
2792,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Allah frees many people on the day of Arafah, and on no other day does He free more people from hell."
2793,"Umar ibn Uthman narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “There are four people whom I, Hal, and the Haram will not give safety to in any place: Hawairat ibn Naqeed, Muqais, Hilal ibn Khatl, and Abdullah ibn Abu Sarh. (The narrator narrates) Hawarith was killed by Sayyidna Ali (RA), Muqis was killed by his cousin, Laha, Hilal bin Khatl was killed by Sayyidna Zubair (RA) As for Abdullah bin Sarh, Sayyidna Uthman (RA) asked for protection for him, he was his foster brother. One was killed and the other survived. He later accepted Islam."
2794,"Umar ibn Uthman narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""You are Saeed. Who is greater among us (the two of us), me or you?"" So they said, I (was born) before you, may God bless you, and you are older than me, and you, may God bless you, are better than me."
2795,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: You should perform Hajj before you cannot perform Hajj. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""The villagers will sit on the edges of their own areas and no one will be able to reach (Mecca) to perform Hajj."""
2796,"Sayyiduna Fazla bin Ubaid (RA) narrates that on the occasion of the Battle of Khyber, a necklace was brought to the Prophet (PBUH) which was plated with gold and had precious stones attached to it. You return it until both of them (i.e. stone and gold) are separated."
2797,"A necklace was brought to the service of Sayyidna Fazla bin Ubaid, may God bless him and grant him peace, which was covered with gold and stones, and the gold and stones were taken off under his orders, and he said, ""Sell the gold and gold in exchange for equal weight."""
2798,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, people used to sell fruits for sale. A narrator named Ibn Mahdi has quoted these words. People used to pledge allegiance for twenty-two years, then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Make salaf in exchange for the prescribed measure and weight."""
2799,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) came to Madinah, people used to sell Salaf for a year and a half, so he said, ""Whoever wants to sell Salaf (loan) should trade for a specified period of time in exchange for a specified measure and a specified weight."" These words of the tradition are from a narrator named Neshapuri, Mohali has quoted these words."
2800,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) came to Madinah, people used to borrow and trade dates for two or three years."
2801,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) came to Madinah, people used to trade on loan for a year or two."
2802,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) came to Madinah, people used to trade fruits on loan for two or three years."
2803,"Makhool narrates this hadith as a hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that whoever buys something that he has not seen, he has the right to accept it when he sees it, and if he wants to, he can leave it. Abu al-Hasan (i.e. Darqutni) says that this hadith is transmitted and its narrator Abu Bakr Maryam is weak."
2804,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words, Ibn Sirin states that even if the thing is not according to the time that the person mentioned to the buyer, this deal will be binding."
2805,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when a person buys something that he has not seen, when he sees it, he will have the right (if he wishes to cancel the deal). This hadith along with some other isnaads has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while some narrators have quoted it as a muqaf tradition up to Ibn Sirin, i.e. as his own words."
2806,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate this on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said, “Whoever buys something, it will be obligatory for him to take it, and he will have the right to terminate the transaction until his partner separates from him."
2807,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that when two men make a deal, each of them will have the right until they separate from each other and live together or one of them gives the other the right."
2808,"The same hadith has been narrated in the same way along with another chain of narrators on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him), however, it is about two parties and the narrator named Ibn Wahib is unique in narrating it."
2809,"Sheikh Abu Wasi narrates: We were participating in a war campaign, while a man came and his horse was with him. One of us said: Will you sell this horse in exchange for this slave? He said: Yes! Then he sold it, then he stayed with us that night, and when morning came, he went to his horse, and our companion said to him: What is your relationship with this horse? Have you not sold it to me? So the man said: I do not need this deal. So our companion said: Now you have nothing to do with it. You have sold it to me. When the people came to them, Sayyidna Abu Barzah said to them both: Are you satisfied with the decision of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace?"
2810,"Shaykh Abu Wasi narrates: We were engaged in a battle, we camped at a place, a man from the army came to us and he was riding his horse, he traded his horse with one of our companions. After that, the narrator has narrated a similar hadith regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Burzah."
2811,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when we used to make a deal with each other, each of the parties would have authority until the two parties to the deal separated from each other. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once me and Sayyidna Uthman made a deal, I sold my land that was in the valley to his land that was in Khyber."
2812,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: A true and trustworthy merchant will be with the martyrs. A narrator named Fazl has quoted these words: On the Day of Resurrection, the Prophets will be with the Siddiqeen and the Martyrs."
2813,Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that a true and trustworthy merchant will be with the righteous prophets and martyrs on the Day of Resurrection.
2814,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this hadith: the price of alcohol is forbidden, the earnings of a prostitute is forbidden, the price of a dog is forbidden, if the owner of a dog comes to you and asks for the price of his dog, fill both his hands with mud, and if the owner of the dog comes to you and asks for the price of his dog, fill both his hands with mud."
2815,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, when Allah Ta'ala declares something haram (this is what it means), He also makes the price of that thing haram."
2816,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Verily, Allah has forbidden wine and its price, and He has forbidden carrion and its price, and He has forbidden pigs and its price."
2817,"Sayyiduna Tamim Dari quotes the saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that it is not permissible to take the price of anything that is not permissible to eat."
2818,"Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyidna 'Uthman, ""When you buy something, measure it with what you buy, and when you sell it, measure it with what you sell."""
2819,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah forbade the sale of grain until it is measured on both sides by the seller and by the buyer.
2820,"Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates that he asked the Messenger of Allah, ""O Messenger of Allah, if I buy and sell, which of the stocks is halal for me and which of the stocks is forbidden for me?"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""My nephew, buy something and do not sell it until you take possession of it yourself."""
2821,"The same hadith is narrated by another Companion, when you do not sell anything to Tulawas until you have measured it."
2822,"Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “Buy something and do not sell it until you measure it."
2823,"Sayyiduna Hakim bin Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah gave him one dinar one day and said, ""Buy a sacrificial animal from it."" He bought a sacrificial animal for one dinar, when he sold it for two dinars, then he bought a sacrificial animal for one dinar."
2824,"Narrated Urwa bin Abul Ja'd: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to know about the merchants' caravan, he gave one dinar to a companion and ordered him to buy a goat for me. So he went and bought two goats for one dinar. When they came with a goat, the Prophet said, May Allah bless your deal. The narrator says (it used to be the case that) I used to stand in a bazaar of Kufa and perform Kamaliya for forty thousand."
2825,"Narrated by Sayyidna Urwa bin Abul Jaid, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to know about the caravan of merchants, so he gave me one dinar. He said, O Urwa, go to those merchants and get a goat from them for one dinar. The narrator says: I went to these merchants and bought two goats for one dinar. Then I brought one goat and one dinar and came to the Messenger of Allah and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is your goat and this is your dinar. Then the Prophet inquired, what have you done? So I narrated the entire incident to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said, ""O Allah, bless his deal."" The narrator says, I remember this very well about myself."
2826,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) forbade bidding.
2827,"Zayd bin Aslam narrates, I heard a man narrating, his name was Shahr, he was a merchant. He asked Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, about the auction, then Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, inquired that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a person to take usury on his brother's bargain (he cannot do this until someone else leaves it), except for the order of booty and inheritance. is different."
2828,This same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar.
2829,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: I bought olive oil in the market, and a man came to me and asked me to give him a higher profit. They do not take it home, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it to be done in this way."
2830,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2831,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, I bought olive oil from the market, when I was making a deal, a man met me and he offered me a higher profit. If the bargain is to be sold at the same place from where it was bought, this cannot be done until the person who trades takes it to his place."
2832,Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of the fruit of a tree until it is ready for use.
2833,"Yunus narrates, I inquired from Shaykh Abu Nad about the traditions mentioned about selling the fruit before it is ripe. Arwah bin Zubair, Sayyidna Sahl bin Hatmah, Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) quoted this statement. Earlier, people used to trade fruit before it was ripe. When such cases appeared in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in abundance, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised those people and said, ""Do not sell the fruit until it is ripe."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said this because there were many disputes and cases These words of the hadith are from the narrator named Aburdad, Sheikh Abu Dawud, may God have mercy on him, says these words that the fruit has become diseased."
2834,"Sayyidna Saeed bin Musaib narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that usury is only in gold, silver, measured, weighed, eaten and drunk things. Imam Darqutni (may Allah have mercy on him) says that this hadith is transmitted and a narrator named Shaykh Mubarak has narrated it as a hadith transmitted to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Imam Malik."
2835,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade the sale of fruit until it is ready for consumption.
2836,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that it is forbidden to sell fruits before they are ripe, unless it is clear whether the fruit will be white or red. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling the milk in the udder and also the wool (on the back of the animal)."
2837,"Sayyidina Abdullah bin Abbas narrated that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of fruit until it is ready to eat, and he also forbade the sale of the wool on the animal's back, the milk in the udder, and the ghee in the milk. A narrator named Waqiyyah has quoted it according to a Mursal tradition with reference to a narrator named Umar Bin Farrukh."
2838,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Do not sell the milk in the udder and do not sell the wool on the back of the animal. This tradition is discontinued.
2839,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may God be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade the sale of what is in the wombs of animals until they give birth, and he forbade the sale of booty until it is divided, and he forbade the sale of charity until it is divided, and he forbade the sale of what comes out after diving."
2840,Sayyiduna Ikrima narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the milk in the udder to be sold for the ghee in the udder.
2841,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade giving allegiance. A narrator named Ayyub has described this. A narrator named Yahya has explained Baighar. He says that Baighar includes trading what the diver brings out after diving. Baighar includes trading a runaway slave or a runaway camel or trading what is in the stomach of animals or trading what comes out of minerals. Or what is in the udders of animals should be traded.
2842,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) forbade the sale of gharar and pebbles.
2843,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Hanzala (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that one dirham of usury that a person eats and eats intentionally is more serious (i.e. worse) for him than committing adultery thirty-six times. This tradition is also transmitted along with a chain of transmission, but it is not transmitted as a hadith."
2844,"Sayyiduna Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that if I commit adultery thirty times, that is more pleasing to me than if I eat a dirham of usury, of which, may Allah know that I ate it, I took it, it was usury. Imam Darqutni (may Allah have mercy on him) says that this hadith is more authentic than the mentioned hadith."
2845,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Hanzalah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that one dirham of usury is a greater sin in the sight of Allah than committing fornication thirty-six times by mistake.
2846,Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) sold a free man who was bankrupt.
2847,"Abd al-Rahman bin Mut'am narrates that my partner bought some dirhams in half, so I said: This is not right, so the man said: I have sold them in the market and no one objected to it. There is nothing wrong with borrowing that will not be fine. You should inquire with Sayyiduna Zayd bin Arqam, for he is the most knowledgeable of all of us about the issues of trade."
2848,"Shaykh Abu Minhal, Sayyidna Bara and Sayyidna Zayd bin Arqam narrate this matter. (That is, dirhams or dinars are being paid on both sides)."
2849,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) and Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrate that the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyidna Sawad bin Ghaziyya, who belonged to Bani Adi. He did not say, O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I have bought good dates for two Sa's and two Sa's for three Sa's. Imam Dar al-Qatni, may God bless him and grant him peace, says that every type of date palm that does not have a specific name is called a collection: It is like there is a collection (of different types of dates) in the land of so-and-so."
2850,This hadith is narrated by Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad bin Abdul Majeed bin Suhail along with another chain of transmission.
2851,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Hurairah and Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri.
2852,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Hurairah and Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA).
2853,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the thing that is weighed should be equal when both of them have the same oath, and when something is found, it should be the same, but when the oaths on both sides are different, then there is nothing wrong with that. The same hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) with regard to other isnads."
2854,"Shaykh Abu Ash'ath narrates that he was present at the sermon of Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit, may God be pleased with him. He narrates that I heard him narrate that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrates that gold should be sold for gold, but it can be done with an equal weight, and silver can be exchanged for silver, but it can be done with an equal weight. He ordered to sell dates for wheat and dates, and salt for salt, and then explained that there is no problem in trading barley for wheat as long as it is hand-to-hand and whatever is more in it, but this transaction should be hand-to-hand, except in cases where the more he gives or takes, it will act as usury. A narrator named Abdullah narrates: I narrated this hadith to my father, and he considered it to be good."
2855,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when there is a dispute between the seller and the buyer, and both of them do not have any evidence, the seller will be sworn in, then the buyer has the choice whether to sell it or not."
2856,"Abdul Malik bin Ubaydah narrates: I was with Abu Ubaydah bin Abdullah two men came to him and they traded one thing and they said: I have bought this thing for so much. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed about the seller, that an oath should be taken from him, after which the buyer will have the right to acquire the item according to the seller's statement and to abandon it if he wishes."
2857,"Abdul Malik bin Jubeer narrates: I was with Abu Ubaidah, the son of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, and two men came to him. They had traded something. One of them said: I have bought this thing for so much. The other said: I have sold this thing for so much. I was present with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when such a case was brought before him, and he ordered that the seller should take an oath, and then the buyer would be given this option whether he took it from him or left it. This tradition is also present along with another document."
2858,"Abd al-Rahman bin Qays narrates this message from his grandfather regarding his father. Sayyidna Ash'ath bin Qais bought a slave from Khums for twenty thousand dirhams from Sayyidna Abdullah. Sayyidna Abdullah gave this message about its price. He said: I have bought it for ten thousand dirhams. Abdullah said: Name someone who can decide between you and me. Sayyidna Ash'at said: You will decide between me and you. It has been heard that when there is a dispute between the parties to the deal and there is no proof between them, then the statement of the owner of the goods will be valid or both of them should abandon the deal."
2859,This tradition is transmitted as a muqaf hadith along with another chain of transmission.
2860,"Abd al-Rahman narrates this statement of his father: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud sold a government slave for twenty thousand, that is, he brought ten thousand to Sayyidna Ash'ath bin Qays, then Sayyidna Abdullah said: I sold it to you for twenty two thousand, then Ash'at said: I did it for ten thousand. I am narrating to you a hadith narrated on the authority of the Messenger of Allah."
2861,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when there is a difference between the two parties to the transaction, the seller's statement will be valid, but if the item has been lost, then the buyer's statement will be valid. The narrator of this tradition, Hasan bin Amara, is obsolete."
2862,"Qasim bin Abd al-Rahman narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of his father on the authority of his grandfather (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him) when there is a dispute between the two parties about the transaction and the goods are in the same state and have not perished, then the seller's statement will be valid or else both of them will terminate the transaction."
2863,The same tradition is also narrated in another document.
2864,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2865,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when there is a dispute between the two men who have traded and the goods sold have been lost, then the seller's statement will be valid. He has narrated this tradition as a marfu' hadith."
2866,"Qasim bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this statement of his father: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud sold a government slave to Ash’ath. They had a dispute about the price. Sayyidna Abdullah said: I sold it to you for twenty thousand. Sayyidna Ash’at said: I bought it from you for ten thousand. Sayyidna Ash'ath said: Sayyidna Abdullah said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that when there is a dispute between two parties to a transaction and the goods sold are in their original condition and both parties do not have any evidence, then the seller's statement will be valid, or both of them will terminate the transaction. Sayyidna Ash'at said: finish"
2867,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a bundle of leaves from a villager. When a deal was made, the Prophet said to him, “You have the power (that if you wish, you can terminate it).” The man said to the Prophet (peace be upon him): May Allah bless your deal. In one hadith, these words are said: The villager said to the Holy Prophet: May Allah settle your business. All the narrators of this tradition are authentic."
2868,"Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) bought something from a villager. I think he was related to Banu Umar bin Sa’sa’ah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a bunch of leaves from him. When the deal was made, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “You can take it if you want.” The villager said: I have not seen such a deal till today, may God Almighty Keep your deals settled! Which tribe do you belong to? So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is from Quraysh."
2869,"Taus narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a bunch of leaves from a villager, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the villager the right to terminate the deal if he wished. The narrator has quoted as per previous tradition."
2870,"A narrator named Amr has narrated this. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) was riding a camel that did not enter Q Abu. It was owned by his father. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar could not pass Q Abu on it. That camel went ahead of the Prophet's camel. Later, he reprimanded him, but that camel did not enter Q Abu. The Prophet (PBUH) said, ""O Umar! Sell me. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought it. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar and said, ""This is yours. Now treat him as you wish."" These words of tradition are from a narrator named Ibn Ibad."
2871,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Barira entered into a contract of writing for herself in exchange for paying Nawaqiyya every year. She came to Sayya Ayesha Siddiqa to help her in this matter. Tusaida Ayesha said, ""No, if you want, I will pay the whole thing at once, but I will have the right to your walaa."" He said: That the right of Wala will remain with them. She came to Sayyida Aisha. Meanwhile, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came. Tubira told Sayyida Aisha in a low voice all the things that she had said to her owners (and the answer they had given). This is what Tusayda Aisha said: No, and I will have the right of Wala, (so I am ready for this matter). Aisha said, ""O Messenger of Allah, Barirah came to me to seek my help regarding her contract of writing. I said: If the owners want, I will pay them all together and the right of ownership will remain with me."" He attains that which liberates. Sayyida Aisha narrates) So I bought him and set him free. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up while giving a sermon to the people, praising Allah and saying: What has happened to the people? The condition that Allah has allowed will be stronger. What has happened to the people, they say that you free so-and-so and the right of ownership will remain with me. The right of ownership belongs to the person who frees. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Berira's husband was a slave, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Berira authority."
2872,"Abdul Wahid bin Ayman narrates this statement of his father: I came to the service of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, I said to her: O Umm al-Mu'minin, I was with Utbah bin Abulhab, (i.e. I was his slave). So he said, ""O my son, I came to Berira. He had made a contract for writing. He said: You buy me. I said: OK. He said: My owners will not sell me until they impose the condition of my walaa. So I said: Then I have no need for you. When the Prophet heard this or it was reported to him, he inquired what Barira was saying. I told you about it. He said, ""You buy him and set him free, and let these people remain as they are, and impose whatever conditions they wish."" (Sayyida Aisha) So I bought him and set him free, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""The right of the freedman belongs to the one who frees him, even if (the people of the other side) impose such conditions."""
2873,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Basheer Saghir had a special place where he used to sit next to the Prophet (PBUH) regularly. Once, the Prophet (PBUH) did not visit him for three days (after three days). I have not seen you for the last three days, so they said, ""My parents are sacrificed to you. I bought a camel from such and such a person. He stayed with me, and after that he became rebellious and ran away. I went after him, (caught him) and handed him over to his owner, so he took him from me."" He said, ""Don't you know that rebellious animals are returned on the same basis?"""
2874,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates a tradition similar to this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The rebellious camel is returned.
2875,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) narrates: I used to trade camels in Baqi, sometimes I would sell them for dinars, and I would receive dirhams instead of dinars, and sometimes I would sell them for dirhams and receive dinars instead of dirhams, which would take its place, and he used to give it away. I said, O Messenger of Allah, I want to ask you a question. I trade camels for profit. Sometimes I sell them for dinars but receive dirhams. Sometimes I sell them for dirhams and receive dinars. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""There is nothing wrong with it if you continue to take it according to the price of that day until the two of you separate or there is no agreement between you."" There is some difference in wording in one tradition."
2876,"Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that gold for gold, silver for silver, dates for silver, dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, salt for salt can only be sold hand-to-hand. be)."
2877,"Muammar bin Abdullah narrates that he sent his slave with a saa of wheat and said: Sell him a saa and bring what he bought through it. The slave went and received a saa and a little more than a saa when he came and told them about it. Umar said: Why did you do this? Go and return it and give only equal religion, because I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Grain for grain. What they meant was that it can only be taken equally, which was our food in those days. The slave said: These are not like it. Toumamar said: I am afraid that they are equal to it."
2878,"It is narrated about Muammar bin Abdullah that he sent his slave with a saa of wheat and said: Sell him a saa and bring what he bought with it. The slave went and received a saa and a little more than a saa when he came and told him about it. Umar said: Why did you interfere with it? Go and return it and give only equal religion, for I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that grain can only be exchanged for grain. The narrator says that our diet used to be in those days, he said to Muammar: He said that they are not like him, so he said, I think that they are like him."
2879,Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the one who takes usury and the one who gives it are equal (sinners).
2880,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that the dinar will be exchanged for the dinar, and the dirham will be exchanged for the dirham for an additional payment."
2881,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said on the occasion of the Farewell Hajj that a Muslim is the brother of another Muslim, for him the blood of his brother or anything from his property is not halal, except what he gives to him according to his choice. Beware! Have I preached? The people said: Yes, the Prophet said, O Allah, be a witness."
2882,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that no one should become a companion to his brother until he gives it to him of his own free will.
2883,"Sayyidna Amr bin Yathirbi narrates that I was present with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the farewell Hajj in Mina. The narrator says) I said at that time, O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about this if I find my cousin's goats in front of me and take one of them and slaughter it, will there be any sin on me in this regard? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""If you come across a goat and at that time you have a knife in your hand and something to bind your hands and feet, do not touch that goat."""
2884,"Sayyidna Amr bin Yathirbi narrates that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, while giving a sermon to us, said, ""Beware that the wealth of his brother is not lawful for any Muslim, except that which he himself chooses to give."" That goat is found in Virana) and at that time you picked up the knife and the equipment for tying the goat, but you could not touch it. Imam Darqutni (may God have mercy on him) says that it has been stated that (Khubat al-Hamish) is a place between Makkah and its suburbs, it is a place where there is no population."
2885,Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that it is permissible for any Muslim to take wealth only by his will.
2886,Sayyiduna Abu Hira al-Raqashi narrates the statement of his uncle that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the wealth of any Muslim can be taken only by his will.
2887,This hadith is also narrated along with another document.
2888,Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the wealth of a believer is as respectable as his life.
2889,"Abdullah Bin Ka'b narrates this statement of his father, once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him and he was confused with one of his debtors. He said, O Messenger of Allah, this is my debt. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired if you do not do this, that is, you should receive half from him. He said this through his blessed hand, and I said yes! O Messenger of Allah, he received half of the share, and left half of the share (the narrator doubts that perhaps the word half has been transferred instead of Shatar in the hadith)."
2890,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that the Muslims will act according to the terms of each other and peace between Muslims is permissible. These words of tradition are from a narrator named Yunus, while other narrators have quoted the word, between people."
2891,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that reconciliation between Muslims is permissible.
2892,Kathir bin Abdullah narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of his father on the authority of his grandfather: The conditions prescribed by the Muslims (will be fulfilled) except for a condition that makes a lawful thing haram or makes a haram thing lawful.
2893,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa cites this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).
2894,Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that the conditions of the Muslims will be obeyed as long as they are in accordance with the truth.
2895,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The charity of a deer is what a man spends on his life on his wife. be done or spent in any sinful act. The narrator says, I inquired from Muhammad bin Mankader, what is meant by this, that a man should protect his honor through it? So he said that he should pay a poet or a foul-mouthed man (so that he would not be rude to him)."
2896,Sayyiduna Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a person who finds his property with a person should take it and the other person will demand it from the person from whom he bought it.
2897,"Sayyidna Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that if a person finds his property with a certain person, he will be more entitled to that property and the other person will go to the person from whom he bought it."
2898,"Sayyidna Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the person who is found to have property in a certain way, he will be more entitled to that property and the person who bought it will go to the person who sold it."
2899,"Sayyiduna Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that if a person finds his property in possession of a particular person, he is more entitled to that property, and the person who had that property will go after the person from whom he bought the property."
2900,"Umar Ibn Khaldah Ansari narrates that we came to the service of Sayyidna Abu Huraira about one of our companions who had been declared bankrupt due to illness. Sayyidna Abu Huraira said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had given this decision about a person who had passed away and was bankrupt. which forms part of this partner)."
2901,"Ibn Khaldah Zarqi, who was a judge of Madinah Munawarah, narrates that we came to the service of Sayyidna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, about one of our companions who had become bankrupt, so Sayyidna Abu Huraira, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that this is a matter about which the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has given a ruling that a person who dies or is declared bankrupt, and then the owner of a certain property finds his property with him, he will be more entitled to that property."
2902,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH) who sells an item, then his partner is declared bankrupt, and the first person finds his item in his possession, and the first person did not receive anything from the price of the item, then the item will be given to that person, but if he had received some of the price, then he will be considered like other creditors."
2903,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a person who sells an item and then goes to a particular person who has been declared bankrupt, and the seller has not received any of its value, then the item will be given to that person, but if he has received some of its value, he will be counted as the other creditors. A narrator named Yaman bin Adi has quoted these words, if this person has paid some of its price, then that other person will be counted like the rest of the debtors."
2904,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the same with regard to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but these words are added. ""A person who dies having the property of another person, whether that person has received any money from his compensation or not, he will be counted like other creditors"". A narrator named Yaman bin Adi has disputed its authenticity."
2905,This tradition is narrated along with another document. A narrator named Yaman bin Adi is weak in hadith.
2906,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""When a person becomes bankrupt and a seller finds the property in his possession, he will have more rights to the property than other creditors."""
2907,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever finds his wealth in the possession of a person who has been declared bankrupt, then he will be more entitled to this wealth than others.” The meaning is the same."
2908,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When you sell a fruit to your brother and some calamity befalls that fruit, then it is not permissible for you to take the wealth of your brother without any right."
2909,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: If you sell some fruit to your brother and some calamity befalls him, then it is not permissible for you to receive any compensation for it. The narrator narrates that I inquired from my teacher Abu Zubair that there are these words in the hadeeth which Aih? So they did not answer."
2910,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another document, it also has the same words. So he said: No."
2911,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever buys (or sells) fruit and a heavenly calamity befalls him, then he does not take anything from it, on what basis will you receive your brother’s property without any right?”"
2912,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a reduction in compensation for the loss caused by a calamity, and he forbade bargaining for a later payment of several years."
2913,"Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) says about a person who pledges something and then it is lost. Sayyidna Umar (RA) says: If it is less than what he was pledged, he will return his full right, and if it is more than that, he will be a trustee."
2914,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned something (regarding a reduction in compensation) due to calamity. Sufyan says I don't know how much reduction you ordered.
2915,"Saeed bin Musaib narrates that the slave of Sayyida Umm Habiba (RA) was declared bankrupt, and he was brought to Sayyidna Uthman (RA), then Sayyidna Uthman (RA) gave this decision about him: The person who received some of his right before he became bankrupt became his, and the person who found his property with him will be more entitled to this property."
2916,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the pledged thing is fully (considered as pledge).
2917,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The pledge is considered as a pledge in its entirety."""
2918,"Sayyiduna Anas, may God be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The pledged thing is with whatever is in it. The narrator of Ismail used to fabricate this hadith, and the narration of this hadith by Qatadah and Hamad bin Salamah is invalid, and God knows best."
2919,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the mortgage is not closed (to the one with whom it is placed), he will receive its benefits and the ransom will also be the responsibility of that person."
2920,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).
2921,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the mortgage is not closed for the person with whom it is kept, he will get the benefit of it and his ransom will be his responsibility."
2922,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH) that the mortgage is not foreclosed, but the person will take the benefit of it and you will have to pay for it."
2923,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that a mortgage is not closed, a person takes advantage of it and the ransom is his responsibility."
2924,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the same with regard to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).
2925,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: A mortgage is not closed, you will get the benefit of it and you will be responsible for paying for it."
2926,"Saeed bin Musaib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the mortgage is not closed, the person takes the benefit and the ransom is his responsibility."
2927,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that the mortgage is not closed, the mortgage is with the person with whom it is placed, that person takes advantage of it and the ransom is also his responsibility."
2928,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that when a horse is pawned, a person can ride on it by paying the expenses, similarly when an animal is pawned, he can milk it."
2929,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that when an animal is pledged, the person with whom it is pledged will be responsible for its fodder."
2930,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that one can ride on a mortgaged animal and milk it.
2931,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the pledged thing is considered as a pledge in its entirety.
2932,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave me a shield jointly with Ammar and Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas. He made us sharers in the things we had taken from the booty of the idolaters.
2933,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that Allah says, “I am with two partners until one of them betrays the other, then when he betrays, I leave between them (i.e., My mercy does not remain with them)."
2934,"Abu Hiyaan Taymi narrates the statement of his father that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Allah's grace is upon two partners as long as one of them does not betray his partner."
2935,"Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying, ""Whoever has entrusted you with a trust, return it to him, and whoever has betrayed you, do not betray him."""
2936,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: To the person who has entrusted you, repay the trust to the person who has betrayed you, do not betray him."
2937,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever entrusts you with a trust, pay back the trust and whoever betrays you, do not betray him."""
2938,"Arwa narrated that there was a dispute between two men belonging to the Ansar about a piece of land. One of them had planted a palm tree there and the land was the property of the other. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a decision that the land would be given to its owner. Nothing can be (forced) on the land of The narrator says that the person who narrated this tradition to me said that he had seen this palm tree which was very tall and whose roots had been cut by an axe. These words of the hadith are not for an oppressor, it means that you go into someone else's land and start farming there (ie do it without his consent)."
2939,"Sayyidna Rafi bin Khadij (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade muhaqla and muzabnah. He (PBUH) said: “There are three types of farming: One is when a person owns land and he cultivates it, a person who is given land as a gift and cultivates it, and a person who rents land in exchange for gold and silver (then he can cultivate it)."
2940,"Hanzalah bin Qais Zarqi narrates that he asked Sayyidna Rafi bin Khadij about renting land, and he said, ""The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade renting land."" So he said, there is no problem in giving it in exchange for gold and silver."
2941,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade giving land on rent, except in exchange for gold and silver (land can be given on rent)."
2942,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the statement of Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa that once the Prophet (PBUH) was going on a journey and he saw a field that was flourishing. Calculate what you have spent in that land and then take it from the owner of the land and hand over that person's land and his field to him.
2943,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the land of Khyber and the palm groves there to the Jews so that they (the Muslims) would pay half of it.
2944,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Khaybar to the people living there on the condition that they would pay half (to the Muslims) of the produce there, be it fruit or agriculture."
2945,"There are these words in a hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) agreed with the people of Khyber that whatever produce there would be, be it fruit or agriculture (they would pay half of it to the Muslims)."
2946,"Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), people used to buy and sell fruits. When it was time to harvest, the debt collector would come and the one who had to pay would say that this time the produce has suffered such and such a disaster. Cultivate till the fruit is ripe and ready. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this as an advice because there was a lot of disagreement among the people about it."
2947,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) agreed with the people of Khyber that they would pay half of the production of dates and crops produced there to the Muslims. The narrators have disagreed about one word of the tradition.
2948,It is narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Umar that he narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allowed the Jews living in Khaybar to work on the lands there on the condition that they would pay half of the produce (to the Muslims) and these portions were fixed.
2949,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the land of Khyber and the palm groves there (to the Jews) on the condition of paying half of the produce. In a tradition, these words were given to the Jews by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
2950,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the land of Khyber (to the Jews) on the condition that they would pay a half share of dates, agriculture, produce and all other (kinds of produce)."
2951,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) temporarily took some armor and weapons from Safwan bin Umayyah on the occasion of the Battle of Hunain. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""It is taken temporarily, which will be returned."""
2952,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather regarding his father that the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) borrowed some weapons from Safwan bin Umayyah, and Safwan asked if it will be returned, O Messenger of Allah! The Prophet (PBUH) said yes."
2953,"Safwan bin Ya'ali narrates the statement of his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when my messenger comes to you, give him this thing. The narrator says, I think he mentioned thirty thousand and thirty camels. Sayyidna Ya'ali bin Umayyah says that I asked, are you taking a loan that will be returned? So the Prophet (PBUH) said yes."
2954,"The same hadith has been narrated along with another document, in which there are these words: I asked, O Messenger of Allah, should you temporarily take those whose ransom will be paid? Or are they taking it temporarily so that they will be returned? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, they will be returned."
2955,"Umayyah bin Safwan narrates the statement of his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him to borrow some armor on the occasion of the Battle of Hunain, so he said, “O Sayyidna Muhammad! What are usurping? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said no, but they are taking them temporarily for which a ransom will also be paid. The narrator narrates that some of his armors were damaged, so the Prophet offered him to take their ransom, so he said that now I have been attracted to Islam and I am more interested in it."
2956,"Umayya bin Safwan narrates that his father narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed some iron armor from me, so I asked, O Messenger of Allah, are they guaranteed? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""These are collaterals. Some of them were lost, so the Prophet said to them, 'If you want, I will give you its ransom.'"""
2957,"Ata has narrated with reference to some people belonging to the family of Abdullah bin Safwan that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Safwan, do you have any weapons? He said, are you taking it temporarily or will you usurp it? After this, the narrator has mentioned the entire hadith."
2958,"A narrator named Abdul Aziz has narrated on the authority of Ata with reference to some people belonging to the family of Sayyiduna Safwan that the Prophet (peace be upon him) temporarily took (some weapons). After that, the narrator mentioned the previous hadith."
2959,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""What is temporarily taken will be returned, and what is given as a donation (for temporary use) will be returned."" So a person said: Is this the decision of the Messenger of Allah? So he said, ""This is the decision of Allah, who has the right to fulfill it."""
2960,"Sayyidna Abu Umamah Bahli (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) say this during his sermon on the occasion of Hajj Al-Wadaa: Allah has determined the right of every possessor, therefore a will cannot be made for an heir. Allah Ta'ala will continue to be cursed by His angels and all humans until the Day of Resurrection. A woman should not spend anything from her husband's house without his permission. It was asked, O Messenger of Allah, not even grain. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""It is our most important wealth."" Then he said, ""What is given for temporary use will be returned, and what is given as a gift for temporary use will also be returned, the duty will be paid, and the person in charge will be obliged to pay the ransom."""
2961,Amr bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather regarding his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that a person who is entrusted with a trust will not be required to pay a ransom.
2962,"Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said to his father, ""Don't make me a witness about adultery."""
2963,"Sayyidna Nu'man (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that his mother said to his father Sayyidna Bashir: That he should give his son Nu'man a garden of dates, so Sayyidna Bashir did so, then he asked who should I make a witness about this? So this woman said: To the Holy Prophet, Sayyiduna Nu'man's father came to the Prophet's service and mentioned this to him. The Holy Prophet said, ""Do you have any other children besides him?"" He said yes! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Have you given it to everyone else in the same way as you have given it to him?"" He said no! So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""A person like me cannot be a witness to such a thing. Allah, the Exalted, likes that you act justly towards your children, just as He likes that you act justly among yourselves."""
2964,"Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that my father gave me a slave as a gift and my mother instructed me to go with him to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so that I could make him a witness on this matter. They said no. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Then take it back."""
2965,This hadith is also narrated along with another document.
2966,"It is narrated about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) that a person called him and wanted to make him a witness regarding his will, so he preferred some of his children over other children in the will, then Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) has forbidden us to be witnesses in an act of transgression. Then Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar (R.A.) walked quickly."
2967,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) both narrate this as a valid hadith that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that it is not permissible for any Muslim to take something back after making a donation, but he can take back what he gives to his children. It is like one who licks his own vomit again after vomiting."
2968,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father and his grandfather: No one can take back what he has given to him, only the father can take back (what was given to him) from his children. The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, but there is some wording difference in it. And this hadith is narrated as Mursal Hadith along with a chain of transmission which has these words: A father can take back his Hiba (from his children)."
2969,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) who does something wrong, then he is more entitled to that thing as long as he does not take any retribution for it. This hadith is not authentically proved to be authentic, but it is true that it is transmitted as a suspended tradition from Sayyiduna Umar on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar."
2970,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that a man is more entitled to his reward until he takes any revenge for it.
2971,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that the one who gives a bribe is more entitled to his bribe as long as he does not take any retribution for it.
2972,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2973,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says, ""A man is more entitled to his reward until he receives any reward for it."""
2974,"Sayyidna Samrah narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that when a man gives a gift to a relative, he should not take it back. The narrator named Abdullah bin Jafar is unique in narrating this tradition."
2975,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who gives something and then wants to take it back, then he will be more entitled to that thing as long as he does not take any revenge for it, but his example will be like a dog that licks its own vomit."
2976,"Sayyidna Tariq bin Abdullah Moharibi (RA) narrates that I visited the Prophet (PBUH) twice. Once I saw him in the market of Dhul Majaz. I was there with my goods which I had kept there for sale. Similarly, when the Prophet (PBUH) passed by, he was wearing a red halwa and he was saying in a loud voice, O people! A man was walking behind you holding a stone, the person who had seriously injured you was saying, O people, do not listen to them because they are lying, so I asked who is this sir? So people said that this is a young man from the descendants of Abdul Muttalib. People said that it was his uncle Abd al-Azi (says the narrator) it was Abul Hab. Then when Islam prevailed and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, we came with some horsemen from Rabdah and the southern areas of Rabdah, and we camped near Madinah. There was a woman with us. We replied from Rabdah and the narrator from the southern areas of Rabdah says that we had red camels with us. They inquired whether you will sell your camels. So we answered yes, they inquired, for how much? We said: In exchange for so many sa's of dates, they did not ask us to make any reduction. Then they took hold of the camel's head and went inside the city and disappeared from our sight. We began to blame each other. I have seen a thing (which proves it) that they will not disgrace you. I have not seen the face of any person like that. You look more like the fourteenth moon than a young one. Then when it was time for Isha, a person came to us and said, ""Peace be upon you. I am the messenger of Allah's Messenger who has come to you. He has instructed you to eat your fill of these dates and measure them completely."" The next day we entered the city of Madinah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing on the pulpit and giving a sermon to the people. He was saying: The giving hand is the upper hand and you start the spending on the person who is under your care, your mother, your father, your sister, your brother and your closest loved one. Then an Ansari stood up and said, O Messenger of Allah, this Banu Taalba, who killed such and such a person in the time of Jahiliyyah. He will not pay ransom on behalf of his children."
2977,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever makes a cash transaction for something, he should not make any change (in the thing given) as payment. Ibrahim bin Saeed says that means he should receive the same thing for which he made a cash deal or pay the same compensation on the condition of which he made a cash deal."
2978,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) says (the narrator says: I think this is the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW)) When you buy a Salaf, do not sell it further until you measure it completely."
2979,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said that the person who pledges allegiance to Salaf should not impose the condition of paying anything other than the agreed payment.
2980,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Banunazir to leave Madinah, some of his people came to serve him and said: We have some duties that have not yet been returned."
2981,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2982,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says that when the Prophet (PBUH) ordered Banun Nazir to be exiled, he said, O Sayyidna Muhammad! We want to take some loans from people, so he said, forgive them and leave here quickly."
2983,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says that when the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, intended to evict Banunazir (from Medina), he said, ""O Messenger of God, you have ordered us to evacuate, while we are about to take loans from people that have not yet been received."""
2984,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when a funeral was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he did not ask about his deeds, but only asked about his debt. When you stood up, you asked your companions whether your companion has any debt. The people asked for two dinars, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from there. He said, ""You should perform the funeral prayer for your companion."" Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, said, ""O Messenger of God, it is my responsibility to pay for both of them. This person is free from both of them."" Just as you have removed the trouble of your brother, whoever dies and owes him a debt, then he is pledged in exchange for that debt, and whoever removes the trouble of the debt of a dead person, Allah will remove the trouble of that person on the Day of Resurrection. So someone asked, is this a special order for Sayyiduna Ali or for all Muslims? He said, ""Rather, it is for all Muslims."""
2985,Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that it is forbidden to (hire) Nirjanur for a couple.
2986,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that grapes should not be sold until they are ripe, and grapes should not be sold until their seeds are ready."
2987,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muzabnah and forbade that fresh dates should be measured and sold in exchange for dry dates.
2988,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade (selling) fresh dates instead of dry dates.
2989,Salim narrates the statement of his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of dry dates for fresh dates.
2990,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade Muhakla, Muzabnah, Mukhabara, and forbade Sunya, but if there is knowledge about it (then the ruling will be different)."
2991,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade trading in an unknown thing until one is aware of it.
2992,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not trade fruits until they are ripe and ready, and do not trade fruits for dates. A"
2993,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) forbade the likes of him.
2994,Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade the lending of dry dates in exchange for dry dates. There is some disagreement about the wording of this tradition.
2995,"Abdullah bin Yazid narrates that Shaykh Abu Ayyash asked Sayyidna Sa'd about two types of wheat (whether they can be traded with each other), then Sayyidna Sa'd (RA) declared it abominable. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about it that when it dries up, it decreases."
2996,"Abdullah bin Zayd narrates that Sheikh Abu Ayyash Zayd told him that he once asked Sayyidna Sa'd (RA) about two types of wheat: Sayyidna Sa'd asked him which of the two types is better. So they replied white ones, then Sayyidna Sa'd (RA) forbade them from doing so. Sayyidna Sa'd said that I asked the Prophet (PBUH) to curse him. People answered yes! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
2997,"Sheikh Abu Ayyash narrates that during the time of Sayyidna Sa'd, men made a deal about two types of barley. Sayyidna Sa'd said that in the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), two men made a deal of dry and fresh dates. The people replied yes, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (Then it is not true)."
2998,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever buys and sells with another, each of them will have the right (to terminate the transaction) until they separate from their place, except in the case where the authority has been given in the transaction, and it is not permissible for a person to separate from his partner under the fear that he will terminate the transaction. will"
2999,This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads.
3000,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement from his father: A man came to the service of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and asked him about a person in the state of Ihram who has intercourse with his wife. He pointed to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and said, ""Go to him and ask him."" The man asked if I should sit down now. He said: No, you go with the people, people who work, you should do the same. Next year, you should come and perform Hajj and bring the sacrificial animal with you. The man came back to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and told him about it. Sayyidna Abdullah said to him, ""You go to Sayyidna Abbas, may God be pleased with him, and ask him."" So Sayyidna Abbas also answered in the same way that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) had answered him. That person came back to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr and told him about what Sayyidna Abbas had answered. Then the person inquired what do you say about it? So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar said, I also give the same answer as what he has described."
3001,This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads.
3002,"Yunus bin Ishaq narrates this statement of his mother Aaliyah, I and Umm Qahba Khatoon went to Makkah. We replied, ""We belong to Kufa. Now Aaliyah is narrating. It is as if Ayesha did not pay attention to us, and Qahbah said to her: O Umm al-Mu'minin, I have a slave girl. I bought her from Sayyidna Zayd bin Arqam Ansari for eight hundred dirhams until he was paid. Then when he decided to sell this slave girl, I bought her for six hundred dirhams in cash. Narrator Khatun narrates that Sayyida Aisha turned to us and said, ""You have done a great deal. You should go and tell Zayd that he has ruined the Jihad he had done with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). However, if he repents, the order will be different. So this lady said to Sayida Aisha: What do you think if I receive my original money from him?"" ""Whoever comes to an admonition from his Lord and turns away before it has already happened, it will be his."" Shaykh states that the women named Qahba and Aaliyah are unknown and their tradition cannot be presented as evidence."
3003,"Shaykh Abu Ishaq Subi'i narrates the statement of his wife. She came to the service of Sayyida Aisha. She was accompanied by the mother of Sayyidna Zayd bin Arqam Ansari, and there was another woman. Tusideh Aisha said, ""You have made a very bad deal. What happened to him (sayyidna Zayd bin Arqam) with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is nullified until he repents (then the ruling will be different)."
3004,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) prescribed tribute according to time.
3005,"Sayyidna Mukhlid bin Khafaf (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a slave was jointly owned by some people and they sold him. One of the partners was absent. When he came and he refused to accept the deal, those people brought their case to Hisham bin Ismail. He gave a decision that the deal would be declared null and void and those people would deal according to the rate of that day and tribute would be collected. Two slaves were sold for this slave. I went to the service of Urwa bin Zubayr and mentioned this to him, and he said, Sayyida Aisha narrated this hadith to me."
3006,"Hamza bin Abdullah narrates this statement of his father, whatever is alive and accumulated at the time of the transaction will be considered as part of the property of the buyer."
3007,"It is narrated about Talha bin Yazid that he discussed some deals with Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “I have not found anything for you that is more comprehensive than what the Prophet (peace be upon him) gave to Hibban bin Munqar. His eyesight was weak, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him permission to cancel the deal for three days. He will keep it and if he likes it, he will take it, if he doesn't like it, he will abandon it."
3008,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Sayyidna Safwan bin Munqar was an old man who had an injury on his head. Because of this, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him the authority to terminate the deal for three days. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: I heard him saying that he used to say Khadaba instead of Khalaba."
3009,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) there was a person who used to buy and sell, and his mental state was found to be defective. Once his family came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, O Prophet of Allah, stop such and such a person from taking possession because he makes a deal, but there is some weakness in his mental state. He said, ""I cannot make a living without buying and selling."" The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said, ""If you must buy and sell, do it."""
3010,"The first hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you must buy and sell, then he said: Do it as it is in exchange for him and there will be no deception. A narrator named Abdul Wahab says that means people will not suffer any loss for him."
3011,"Nafi narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) told him that an Ansari had a stutter in his tongue and he always made a loss in dealings with him. It is narrated about Sayyidna Munqar bin Amr that he had an injury on his head which affected his language, and his mental state also changed somewhat. He used to trade and he always lost money in trade. You will have authority for three days, if after three days you agree, then keep it and if you don't like it, return it to the owner. The life of these Companions was very long. They lived for thirty-two years during the time of Sayyidna Uthman, when people spread everywhere and the number of people also increased, and there used to be a good deal in the market. At that time, they used to buy and sell in the market."
3012,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that the power lasts for three days.
3013,"Hibban bin Waseet narrates this statement of his father regarding his father, when Sayyiduna Umar was appointed as the caliph, he said: O people, I have examined this matter and I have found that the thing that is most similar to your deals in the time of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the authority, which the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave to Hibban bin Munqidh for three days, and this incident happened regarding a slave."
3014,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Makkah is Haram, it is forbidden to sell the land here and it is forbidden to rent the houses here."
3015,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Allah has appointed Makkah as a Haram. Selling the land here and its price is eating Ihram."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also said that whoever eats anything from the rent of houses in Makkah will eat fire. Imam Abu Hanifah, may God have mercy on him, has narrated this tradition as a suspended tradition, but he has had an illusion in it. The second illusion he has had is that he has narrated the name of the narrator as Ubaidullah bin Abu Zayed, although he is Ibn Abi Ziyad."
3016,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) says that whoever eats the rent of the houses of Makkah puts fire in his stomach (this hadith is suspended).
3017,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) says, “Whoever eats the rent of the houses of Makkah (after this is according to the previous hadith)."
3018,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Makkah, Manakh, the land here cannot be sold and the houses cannot be rented. The narrator named Ismail bin Ibrahim is weak, and no one else narrated this hadith except him."
3019,"Sayyidna Alqamah bin Nadla (RA) says that during the time of the Prophet (PBUH) and Sayyidna Umar (RA), whoever was in need would stay there, and whoever did not need it, he would let someone else stay there."
3020,"The same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but this is added in it, it used to be the same during the era of Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him)."
3021,"Sayyidna Alqamah bin Nadla (may God be pleased with him) Kanani narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet, Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar (may God be pleased with him), the houses of Makkah were given away to people and they were not sold."
3022,"Mus'ab bin Sa'd narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him) when Makkah was conquered, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave safety to all except four men and two women. Sababah, Abdullah bin Saad bin Abu Sarh."
3023,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that on the occasion of the conquest of Makkah, when the Prophet (PBUH) left for Makkah, he said to Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA), call the Ansar and bring them! So they announced, O Ansar! Attend the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Ansar came as they had come under a pre-arranged meeting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Go along this path. Whoever tries to come in front of you, kill him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed. Allah blessed him with victory. Then he went up to Safa and addressed the people. At that time (the Ansar) were in the lower part of the hill, one of them said to his companion: Now the love of his people has been highlighted in his heart and he has become attached to his town. The people of the Ansar told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this through revelation, and he said, O Ansar! You said this: Now the love of the nation has been highlighted in the heart of this gentleman and he has developed an attachment to his village. Then you said who am I? By Allah, I am indeed a servant of Allah and I am His Messenger. My life and my death are with you. The Ansar said, O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, we said this only out of fear that you, may God bless you, would not separate from us."
3024,"Abdullah bin Rabah narrates that we went as a delegation to Sayyiduna Muawiyah (RA) and with us was Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) one of us would prepare the food and then invite his companions. On the occasion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with the army on the right side and on the left. When I called them, they came walking fast. Tomorrow, when these obscene people of Quraysh come before you, you have to grind them. We will meet you on Safa (hill). The narrator narrates that he signaled with his hand, the next day the person who tried to come for the contest was killed by Mard or the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was granted victory. If the Quraysh continue to be killed in this way, after today there will be no sign of the Quraysh. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe, whoever closes the door of his house is safe. Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that some of the Ansar said: Now the love of his people has become evident in his heart, and he has developed an attachment to his town, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) revealed several revelations about this. I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. I migrated to Allah and to you. My life and my death are with you."
3025,Sarq says: I had to give some property of a person (the narrator doubts that these are the words) I had to give a loan to a person. That person took me to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The two sons of Zayd bin Aslam have narrated it differently.
3026,"Abd al-Rahman and Abdullah, the sons of Zayd bin Aslam, narrate this on the authority of their father. They participated in a battle. They heard a person calling another person in a loud voice, O thief, O thief. So he told me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me this name. I bought a camel from a villager, then I hid from him. I lost the value of the camel. The villager was looking for me, and people said to him: Go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and tell him about this. I bought a camel and then he hid from me. I could not find him. The Prophet said, ""Look for him. The narrator narrates that this man found me and took me to the service of the Prophet. He said, O Messenger of Allah, this is the person who bought the camel from me and hid from me. The Prophet said, 'You pay the price.' It has been lost. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""You are a thief!"" Then he said to the villager, you go and sell it in the market and get the price of your camel, so this villager made me stand in the market and the price I was charged, he asked the buyer, what are you going to do with it? He said I will free him, so this villager freed me."
3027,"Zayd bin Aslam narrates: I saw an old man in Alexandria whose name was Sarq. I inquired what this name was. So they told me that this name was given to me by the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I will not give it up. So he said, I came to Madinah and I told the people that my wealth is coming. Those people made some deals with me. I had to pay them. That wealth was lost from me. Those people took me to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. He said, ""You are a thief!"" Then you sold me for four camels, these creditors asked the buyer what will you do with it? He told that I will free him, so these people said: We also need reward as much as you, so these people together freed me, but my name remained."
3028,"Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the occasion of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked before entering Makkah, O Messenger of Allah, where will you stay or in your house? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Has Aqeel (bin Abu Talib) left us any house (because) a disbeliever does not inherit a Muslim and a Muslim does not inherit a disbeliever."
3029,"Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: It was asked, O Messenger of Allah, where will you camp tomorrow? If Allah willed (the narrators narrate) this is the occasion of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Has Aqeel left anything for us as an inheritance (after this is according to the previous hadith)."
3030,"Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates, He said, O Messenger of Allah, will you stay in your house in Makkah? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Has Aqeel left us any desired place?"" (The narrator narrates) Mr. Aqeel was the heir of Mr. Abu Talib. Ibn Shihab explains that the scholars take this meaning from this statement of Allah: ""Those who believed and migrated, Jihad is this verse up to this point, there is nothing in their Wilayat."""
3031,"The same hadith is narrated from Zuhri, however, these words are added in it (the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace), said: We will camp in Khaif Bani Kinana, where the Quraysh had taken an oath to remain steadfast in disbelief."
3032,"Abdullah bin Zayd narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father. Abdullah and Ubaidullah, the two sons of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) passed by Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) who was in Iraq (performing the duties of the governor). These two gentlemen were coming from the land of Iran. I wish I had something (the narrator doubts that maybe these are the words) I wish I had power over something (that I could give you) Yes, I have accumulated this wealth, take it, buy goods with it, when you go to Sayyidna Umar, then sell it, the profit is yours and pay the original amount to you Sayyidna Umar. The narrator narrates that when these two gentlemen appeared in the service of Amirul Momineen, he asked them if Abu Musa had treated the children of all the emigrants in the same way. They both answered no! So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, Ameerul Momineen will not declare it as valid, he gave it as a loan."
3033,"Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam, may Allah be pleased with him, the Companions of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, when he gave something to a person, used to impose on him the condition that you will not give my property to any living being, do not take it on a sea voyage, do not take it and camp in a waterway."
3034,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) permitted us thirty horsemen to go on an expedition. We encamped near an Arab tribe (settlement). The narrator narrates that the chief of the tribe was bitten (by a poisonous animal). They came to us and inquired whether any of you can survive the bite of a scorpion. The narrator narrates I replied yes I can, but I will not do so until you people pay us (his compensation). He said: We will give you thirty goats (as compensation for him). He came to the service of Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him) and mentioned this to him, so he asked, ""How did you know that it also has a tail?"" (I replied, you have told me) So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Divide them and keep my share with you."
3035,"The same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however the narrator named Shuba has narrated something different in it."
3036,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that some of the companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) came to an Arab tribe and they did not show hospitality to them. So these people fixed a herd of goats as a compensation, so they started reciting the Fatiha while they were sleeping. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said, ""How do you know that there is breath through it?"" You use them and keep my share in them."
3037,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may God be pleased with him) narrates that once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition led by Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) and he passed by a town whose chief was bitten by a poisonous animal. When a person wants to die, our leader is dying, Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Khudri said: I came to him and I recited Surah Fatiha and breathed on him, and he recovered. Those people sent food to us and sent goats. How did you know that it also has a tail? I said, O Messenger of Allah, this matter came to my mind, so the Prophet said, ""Eat (the meat of) these goats and feed us from it as well."""
3038,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates that once some companions were going somewhere, a man came to them and said: The chief of this tribe has been bitten by a poisonous animal. Those companions said: Have you received the reward of the Book of Allah? These companions did not take anything from what they had received as compensation. When these people came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they told him, O Messenger of Allah, that he has received compensation for the Book of Allah. They also told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what they had done (i.e. recited Surah Al-Fatiha). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How did you know that it also has a tail? That is, of Surah Al-Fatihah, then he said, ""Of all things that you receive compensation for, the most entitled is the Book of Allah."" This hadith has been narrated in Sahih."
3039,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that some of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by an Arab tribe whose member had been bitten (by a poisonous animal). Those companions said: Have you received the reward of the Book of Allah? These companions did not take anything from what they had received as compensation. When these people came to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him), they told him, O Messenger of Allah, that he had received compensation for the Book of Allah, so they also told the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, O Messenger of Allah. We passed by an Arab tribe whose member had been bitten (by a poisonous animal). If he recited the book of Allah and breathed on it on the condition, then he was cured. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The book of Allah is the most entitled of all things that you receive compensation for. This hadith is authentic and has been narrated by Imam Bukhari, may God have mercy on him, on the authority of Saydan bin Mudarib, from Abu Mushar."
3040,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that some prisoners were brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He ordered me to sell two of them. I sold them and separated them (i.e. sold them to two separate men).
3041,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me two slaves who were both brothers. I sold one of them. I said, I have sold one of them, so you said, take it back."
3042,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates that he separated a woman and her son while selling, and the Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to cancel the deal. A narrator named Uthman narrated that he had made a separation between a slave girl and her son, and the Prophet forbade him to do so, so he annulled the deal."
3043,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when prisoners were brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he used to give the whole house to them (someone), just like those people used to be, and he did not separate them."
3044,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that the person who separates is cursed. Narrator Abu Bakr narrates that these words are ambiguous, for us it means to separate a prisoner from his offspring."
3045,Sayyidina Abu Musa al-Ash'ari narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade making a distinction between brothers or parents and children (while selling slaves or concubines).
3046,Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the person who (by selling slaves and maidservants) makes a distinction between a mother and her children or brothers.
3047,"Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever separates a mother from her children (by selling slaves and maidservants), Allah will separate that person and his friends on the Day of Resurrection."
3048,Harith bin Salim narrates this statement of his father: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a person who discriminates between fathers and children among prisoners.
3049,"Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade the separation between the mother and her children (while selling slaves and maidservants). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said until the boy becomes an adult and the girl does not menstruate. There is, indeed, a narrator named Abdullah, and it is weak, Ali bin Madani has accused him of being a liar, and none other than him has narrated the hadiths regarding Saeed bin Abdul Aziz."
3050,"Aban narrates that Amir al-Shaabi narrated this hadith to him: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever takes an animal whose owners cannot feed it and leaves it open to graze, then he takes the animal and gives it life (i.e. provides food), then it will be his property. There are also these words in Aban's narration, Ubaidullah says, I inquired about whom he narrated this hadith. So he replied, with reference to several Companions (this hadith has been narrated), this tradition narrated by Hamad is more clear and complete."
3051,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the occasion of the conquest of Khyber, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that booty should be sold before it was distributed, and that pregnant women should not have sex before they give birth to their children. (On this occasion, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the meat of domesticated donkeys and the meat of wild animals."
3052,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr bin As (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to provide supplies for the army. He bought a camel, on the condition that when the person receiving the charity came, the cost of the ride would be paid."
3053,"Amr bin Harish narrates I asked Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr, we live in a place where dinars and dirhams are not customary. So he said, ""You have asked a person who knows about this. Once, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave camels from the camels of Sadaqat for war until the camels were exhausted, but some people were left who did not have animals to ride. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'You buy for us some camels, which will be in exchange for the young camels that will be received as Sadaqah, and when the Sadaqah comes, we will pay those people.' The narrator says) So I bought a camel in exchange for twenty-two young camels, until I was exhausted, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid for it from the camels of Sadaqah."
3054,Amr ibn Harish narrated this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to provide equipment for an army and the camels ran out.
3055,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed them to provide supplies for the army. When the camels became scarce, he instructed us to get one camel in exchange for two camels from the charity camels."
3056,"Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad Sa'idi (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade selling meat in exchange for an animal. Yazid bin Marwan is unique in quoting this tradition from Imam Malik, along with this chain of command, and he has not been followed."
3057,Saeed bin Musayyib narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling animals in exchange for meat. Ibn Musayyib narrates that it is forbidden to sell animals in exchange for meat.
3058,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade selling an animal on loan in exchange for an animal.
3059,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of an animal (in exchange for an animal).
3060,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade making a loan in return for a loan.
3061,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this tradition about the Holy Prophet (PBUH) that he (PBUH) forbade the trading of wood for wood. Ahl lexicographers have explained this, it means making a loan deal in exchange for a loan."
3062,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade using the price of cats and dogs.
3063,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the use of the price of a cat.
3064,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that three things are forbidden, the income of a stalker, the income of a prostitute, and a dog's prey. One of the narrators of this hadith) Walid bin Ubaidullah, is weak."
3065,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog and a cat, but the order for a trained dog (i.e. a hunting dog) is different. A narrator of this tradition) Hasan bin Abu Ja'far is weak."
3066,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that three things are forbidden: the income of a stalker, the compensation of a woman who commits adultery is forbidden, and the price of a dog is forbidden. One of the narrators of this hadith (Musthini, is weak."
3067,"Abu Zubair, quoting Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) says, I think he must have mentioned this with reference to the Prophet (PBUH), he forbade the price of dogs and cats, but the ruling on hunting dogs is different."
3068,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that it is forbidden to (use) the price of a dog and a cat, but the ruling on a hunting dog is different."
3069,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that it is forbidden to (use) the price of a dog and a cat, but the ruling on a hunting dog is different. Hammad did not mention that this hadith was transmitted from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and this hadith is more authentic than the previous one."
3070,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that whoever buys an animal in Misrata will have the right for three days.
3071,The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA).
3072,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) and Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) have narrated this as a valid hadith (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) said, “A citizen should not bargain for a villager, do not buy goods on the way (before the caravan reaches the market), do not make artificial bids, do not place a price against that of your brother, and do not send a message in comparison with your brother’s message of marriage until that other person Do not marry or destroy this message. No woman should demand the divorce of her sister (Sukan) in order to obtain the benefits of her (Sukan) share through her, because that woman will get what is due to her. Can be done."
3073,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (in the same deal) salaf and sale are two conditions in one deal. Dealing with something that is not in one's possession, the profit of which one is not responsible for the guarantee (all these things) are not permissible."
3074,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that an urban person should not make a bargain for a villager. I give a saa of dates, not of wheat."
